ff802-ucm-profile
=================

ALSA UCM profile for the original RME Fireface 802 in class compliant mode:
six stereo outputs and one stereo input as separate PipeWire devices.

Status: the profile is evaluated correctly by alsa-lib with the real card
(host test T1). The physical channel assignment is not yet verified
(hardware test T2). Do not rely on the output names before T2.

Files
-----

  /usr/share/alsa/ucm2/USB-Audio/RME/Fireface-802.conf       profile
  /usr/share/alsa/ucm2/USB-Audio/RME/Fireface-802-HiFi.conf  SplitPCM devices
  /usr/share/alsa/ucm2/USB-Audio/conf.d/0424-3fdd.conf       selection, refuses the 802 FS
  /usr/share/ff802-ucm/longname-master.conf                  master file for the binding
  /usr/sbin/ff802-ucm-bind                                   device binding

No file of alsa-ucm-conf is changed.

Why a device binding
--------------------

alsa-lib before 1.2.16 never loads USB-Audio/conf.d/<vid>-<pid>.conf
(optional include bug, upstream commit 62c24074). ucm.conf does probe
conf.d/USB-Audio/<card long name>.conf before USB-Audio.conf. The package
therefore links exactly this file for the connected card:

  /usr/share/alsa/ucm2/conf.d/USB-Audio/RME Fireface 802 (<serial>) at usb-<port>, high speed.conf
      -> ../../../../ff802-ucm/longname-master.conf

The long name contains the USB port. On another port or hub the profile is
not active (the card keeps its previous profiles) until it is bound again.

Installation
------------

  1. Read "Volume safety" below.
  2. Connect the Fireface 802 in CC mode.
  3. sudo apt install ./ff802-ucm-profile_<version>_all.deb
     The postinst binds the card if exactly one original Fireface 802 is
     connected. Without a card, run 'sudo ff802-ucm-bind bind' later.
  4. sudo ff802-ucm-bind status
  5. Reconnect the Fireface (PipeWire/WirePlumber pick up UCM changes when
     the device appears). The postinst does not restart any service.

Volume safety
-------------

When the profile becomes active, the card switches to the HiFi profile and
six new sinks appear; running streams may move to "Headphones 9/10".
Before reconnecting the Fireface: headphone knobs fully down, headphones
off, amplifiers off, all playback stopped. Then mute all new sinks before
the first playback (docs/audio_ucm.md, "Lautstärkesicherheit vor T3").

Other USB port, other Fireface
------------------------------

  sudo ff802-ucm-bind bind      binds the currently connected card (additional
                                binding; old bindings stay until unbind)
  sudo ff802-ucm-bind unbind    removes all bindings made by this tool

Update
------

  sudo apt install ./ff802-ucm-profile_<new version>_all.deb

Bindings survive upgrades; they point to the master file, which the new
version replaces. With alsa-lib >= 1.2.16 the binding is no longer needed:
'ff802-ucm-bind status' says so; 'sudo ff802-ucm-bind unbind' removes it,
and USB-Audio/conf.d/0424-3fdd.conf then selects the profile on its own.

Removal
-------

  sudo apt remove ff802-ucm-profile    removes the profile and all bindings
  sudo apt purge ff802-ucm-profile     also removes /var/lib/ff802-ucm

Links or files in conf.d/USB-Audio that were not created by ff802-ucm-bind
are never touched.
